  "sport": "bandy",
  "title": "4 v 3 – play your way through",
  "description": "Four blue attackers start with the ball at the halfway line and try to play past three red defenders and score against the goalkeeper. Set up two cone gates just inside the halfway line, one by each board. If red win the ball, they counter and score by taking the ball through one of the gates.\n\nThe attackers look for the player between the defenders, turn and play in the one running in behind. Offside applies, so the run in behind must be timed against the last defender. Switch players after 6–8 attacks and rest between goes. Too hard: play 4 v 2. Progression: the wide player may get past with a wall pass off the boards or skate down and play a cross. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "Take up a position between the defenders, where you can get the ball and turn."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "If there is free ice in front of you – skate with the ball and draw a defender."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "Create two against one where the ball is."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "If you lose the ball – win it back before red reach the gates."
    }
  ],
